CAT = "zapsiraLaw"; SEG = "LAW"
# Private Security Industry Regulation Act 56 of 2001 (as published, Government Gazette 23051,
# 25 January 2002): ss. 2, 3, 20, 21, 23, 25, 28, 43 and the Schedule of offences.
Q = [
("Which body regulates the private security industry in South Africa?",
 "PSIRA", ["SAPS", "The SETA", "The Department of Labour"],
 "The Private Security Industry Regulatory Authority (PSIRA) was established by section 2 of Act 56 of 2001 to regulate the industry. SAPS is the public police service, not the regulator."),
("Which Act set up the Private Security Industry Regulatory Authority?",
 "Act 56 of 2001", ["Act 51 of 1977", "Act 85 of 1993", "Act 92 of 1987"],
 "The Private Security Industry Regulation Act 56 of 2001 created PSIRA. Act 51 of 1977 is the Criminal Procedure Act and Act 92 of 1987 was the old Security Officers Act."),
("The Private Security Industry Regulation Act repealed which earlier law?",
 "The Security Officers Act", ["The Criminal Procedure Act", "The Trespass Act", "The Firearms Control Act"],
 "Section 43 of Act 56 of 2001 repealed the Security Officers Act 92 of 1987,."),
("A friend offers you paid weekend work guarding a car park. What must you have before you start?",
 "PSIRA registration", ["A first aid certificate only", "A letter from the car park owner", "A Grade 12 certificate"],
 "Section 20 of the Act says no person may render a security service for payment, reward or benefit unless registered with PSIRA as a security service provider."),
("Under the Act, which of these counts as rendering a security service?",
 "Protecting property for a fee", ["Locking your own front gate", "Calling 10111 as a bystander", "Watching a neighbour's house free"],
 "The Act defines a security service to include protecting or safeguarding a person or property in any manner, done for remuneration, reward, a fee or benefit."),
("What is the minimum age to register with PSIRA as a security officer?",
 "18 years", ["16 years", "21 years", "25 years"],
 "Section 23(1)(b) requires a natural person applying for registration to be at least 18 years of age."),
("Which citizenship requirement does section 23 set for a person registering as a security officer?",
 "Citizen or permanent resident", ["Citizen by birth only", "Any valid work visa holder", "Any SADC passport holder"],
 "Section 23(1)(a) requires the applicant to be a South African citizen or to have permanent resident status in South Africa."),
("Before PSIRA can register a new security officer, the applicant must have met which requirement?",
 "The prescribed training", ["Two years' work experience", "A valid driving licence", "A firearm competency"],
 "Section 23(1)(c) requires the applicant to have complied with the training prescribed for registration. Firearm competency is a separate matter and only for armed work."),
("An applicant was convicted of theft three years ago. Under section 23, why may registration be refused?",
 "Theft is a Schedule offence", ["Theft is never a bar", "Only violent crimes count", "Only offences abroad count"],
 "Section 23(1)(d) bars an applicant found guilty of an offence listed in the Act's Schedule, which includes theft. As published in 2002 the bar covers the 10 years before the application; the Amendment Act 18 of 2014, once it comes into operation, removes that time limit. Either way a recent theft conviction counts."),
("Which mental health requirement does section 23 place on an applicant?",
 "Being mentally sound", ["A yearly psychologist report", "No requirement at all", "A doctor's note each shift"],
 "Section 23(1)(g) lists being mentally sound among the requirements for registering a natural person."),
("A former SANDF soldier applies to register with PSIRA. What extra document does the Act require?",
 "A clearance certificate", ["A letter from a commander", "A copy of a service medal", "Nothing extra is needed"],
 "Section 23(1)(f) requires a former member of any official military, security, police or intelligence force to submit a prescribed clearance certificate."),
("What must every applicant for PSIRA registration submit with the application under section 21?",
 "A full set of fingerprints", ["A passport photo only", "A recent bank statement", "A reference from a client"],
 "Section 21(1)(a) requires a clear and complete set of fingerprints taken in the prescribed manner, along with the fee and other required documents."),
("A security company is being registered. Who must also be registered with PSIRA?",
 "Its directors and managers", ["Only its armed officers", "Only the owner's family", "Its clients' own staff"],
 "Section 20(2) says a security business may be registered only if every person performing executive or managing functions, and every director, member or partner, is registered."),
("After registering a security officer, what does PSIRA issue to that natural person?",
 "An identification certificate", ["A firearm licence card", "A police appointment card", "A tax clearance certificate"],
 "Section 25 provides for a certificate of registration and, for natural persons, a certificate of identification, the card an officer carries."),
("PSIRA withdraws an officer's registration. What must the officer do with the identification certificate?",
 "Return it to PSIRA", ["Keep it as a souvenir", "Give it to the employer", "Use it until it expires"],
 "The Act requires a person whose registration is withdrawn or suspended to return the certificate of identification or registration to the Authority forthwith."),
("Who is bound by the Code of Conduct for Security Service Providers?",
 "Every security provider", ["Only armed officers", "Only Grade A officers", "Only company owners"],
 "Section 28(2) makes the code of conduct legally binding on all security service providers, and, to the extent the Act provides, on people who use their own employees for in-house security."),
("Which of these is one of PSIRA's main objects under section 3 of the Act?",
 "Set conduct standards", ["Prosecute criminal cases", "Issue firearm licences", "Run police stations"],
 "Section 3 includes determining and enforcing minimum standards of occupational conduct and promoting high training standards. Prosecution belongs to the NPA."),
("PSIRA's objects include promoting a private security industry that acts in line with which document?",
 "The Constitution", ["The client's contract", "The company's tender", "The union's rules"],
 "Section 3(a) requires PSIRA to promote a legitimate industry that acts according to the principles of the Constitution and other applicable law."),
("A guard is found guilty of improper conduct under the Act. For how long can that count against a later registration?",
 "Five years", ["One year", "Ten years", "Twenty years"],
 "Section 23(1)(e) requires that the applicant was not found guilty of improper conduct under the Act within five years before the application."),
("A mall uses its own employees, not a contractor, to guard its stores. Does the code of conduct reach this in-house security?",
 "Yes, as the Act provides", ["No, it is not a contractor", "Only for armed staff", "Only after a complaint"],
 "Section 28(2) extends the code, as the Act provides, to people who use their own employees to protect their own property or people on their premises."),
("Which of these offences is listed in the Act's Schedule of offences that affect registration?",
 "Fraud", ["A parking fine", "Driving with a lapsed licence", "Late tax filing"],
 "The Schedule to Act 56 of 2001 lists offences such as fraud, theft, robbery, assault with intent to cause grievous bodily harm and dishonesty offences."),
("What kind of body does section 2 of the Act establish PSIRA as?",
 "A juristic person", ["A police unit", "A private company", "A trade union"],
 "Section 2 establishes the Private Security Industry Regulatory Authority as a juristic person, a legal body in its own right. It is neither part of SAPS nor a private company."),
("A client asks you to work as a guard while your PSIRA registration is suspended. What is the right response?",
 "Refuse until it is restored", ["Work but stay out of sight", "Work under a colleague's card", "Work for half the rate"],
 "A suspended officer may not render a security service. Using another officer's identification would also be dishonest and an offence."),
("The code of conduct requires minimum standards for security employees in which other area besides conduct?",
 "Minimum wages", ["Uniform colours", "Holiday destinations", "Their home security"],
 "Section 28(3)(b) says the code must ensure payment of minimum wages and standards that prevent exploitation or abuse of security employees."),
]
